\begintext

   GM values (km^3/s^2) consistent with the DE442 planetary ephemeris.

   Source: NAIF, generic_kernels/spk/planets/de442_tech-comments.txt
   (Feb 2025), table 'Mass parameter (GM) for Sun, Moon, and Planets'.
   Converted from its AU^3/day^2 column with AU = 149,597,870.7 km and
   day = 86,400 s; the result matches that table's km^3/s^2 column to
   its printed precision (worst 2.9e-11 relative).

   NAIF publishes gm_de440.tpc but no gm_de442.tpc; this file fills that
   gap so DE442 positions are used with DE442 masses. Numbering follows
   gm_de440.tpc: DE's GM3 is the Earth (399), GMB the Earth-Moon
   barycentre (3), GMM the Moon (301), GM1/2 both barycentre and planet
   for Mercury and Venus (no moons). Generated for digital-orrery.

